course: dictionary
lesson: 9014
title: Informal words: skint
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: "Skint" is a casual, slang word used mostly in Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand. It means having no money at all, or broke. Look at the context: «Can't, I'm skint» is what Jodie says when she cannot buy a hot chocolate.
explain: Use the clues. The speaker says «Can't» before «I'm skint», so being skint is the reason she cannot buy something. If you swap in "I have no money", the sentence still makes sense, so skint must mean broke.
explain: Skint is informal, so you would say it to friends, not write it in a formal letter. It is not rude, but in school writing use a formal word like "short of money" instead.
explain: Many families are short of money at some time, so being skint is nothing to be ashamed of. If a friend says they are skint, be kind and do not make a joke of it.
fact: Skint means having no money at all; broke.
fact: "Skint" is slang, used mainly in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: People often say they are skint near the end of the week or month, when their money has run out.
fact: Other ways to say it include "flat broke", "hard up" and "short of money".
fact: Skint is casual, not rude, but save it for chatting with friends rather than formal writing.
exercise: «Can't, I'm skint.» What does skint mean? | Very happy with a big prize | *Having no money at all | Cold and wet from the rain | Full of energy after a long walk
exercise: Which phrase means about the same as skint? | *Flat broke | Wide awake | Full of joy | Very tall
exercise: Ella says «I'm skint» in the shop. What does she mean? | *She has no money left | She wants to buy a new shirt | She is going swimming | She has lots of spare cash
test: What is a kind way to respond when a friend says they are skint? | Ask them to pay for your lunch | Ignore them because it is their problem | Tell everyone in the class about it | *Be understanding and do not make a joke of it
test: Which of these is the best formal alternative to "skint" in a school essay? | *Short of money | Minted | Broke as a joke | Loaded
exam: Jodie buys Hollie a hot chocolate every Saturday, until one week she says «Can't, I'm skint». Why can't Jodie buy it that week? | She does not like hot chocolate | *She has no money left | She is too tired to walk to the shop | She has already drunk three
